---
import FlowDetail from '../FlowDetail.astro';
import detailResourcePopover from '../../../assets/flow/details/detail-resource-popover.webp';
---
<section class="border-t border-border/60 bg-surface-raised/30 px-6 py-14 sm:py-20" aria-labelledby="tour-resources">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
      <p class="of-eyebrow" data-animate="rise">What it is using</p>
      <h3 id="tour-resources" class="of-display scroll-mt-28 mt-4 text-[clamp(1.85rem,3.4vw,2.75rem)]" data-animate="lead">See what the run asks of your Mac.</h3>
      <p class="of-lede mx-auto mt-5" data-animate="rise">Processor, memory, whole-Mac graphics use, heat, the loaded model, tokens, and running cost appear in one readout while Flow works.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mx-auto mt-11 grid max-w-5xl items-center gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[0.78fr_1.22fr]" data-animate="plate">
      <FlowDetail src={detailResourcePopover} alt="Flow's What Flow is using popover during a benchmark: CPU, memory, and GPU for the whole Mac, Flow's own memory share, tokens and spend for this session and all time, and that the Mac reports cool." caption="Whole-Mac usage · Flow's own share · Tokens and spend, this session and all time" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 20rem, calc(100vw - 3rem)" glow />
      <ul class="flow-list">
        <li>Flow's own footprint sits beside the model's.</li>
        <li>Graphics is labeled for the whole Mac; macOS exposes no honest per-process figure.</li>
        <li>Local tokens accrue while the charge remains absent because nothing was billed.</li>
        <li>Heat uses the Mac's own Cool, Warm, Hot, or Too hot verdict.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <p class="of-spec-fine mx-auto mt-8 max-w-3xl text-center uppercase tracking-[0.14em]">Captured during one live local run on an M3 Max. The figures describe that machine, not a typical result.</p>
  </div>
</section>
